host macOS clone (Mac hand) -- Eastern (EDT) one-clock
title the kernel lays this out -- nineteen modules stop spelling Linux's sockaddr
prompt kg here as Sound. The booked lap: the socket-table fold, %288's named class.
think The parked branch sound/socket-dialect-nineteen already held the option-constant half -- 43 literal declarations across the nineteen moved onto c.SOL and c.SO, with SO_BINDTODEVICE alone reaching std.os.linux because std.c publishes no such option -- so that commit and its session-log sibling were cherry-picked whole rather than rewritten, the index conflict woven by stamp. My half was the layout: nineteen surveyed by nineteen parallel readers against the repaired exemplar, and the shape came back uniform -- a six-line extern struct in Linux's layout, a constructor writing only sin_port, one discarded setsockopt return each, bind already checked. One central transform swapped every struct for const sockaddr_in = c.sockaddr.in under the kernel-lays-this-out comment, rewrote each constructor to the .port/.addr form with the loopback bit-cast, and turned every discarded SO_REUSEADDR and SO_RCVTIMEO return into a named-error check with its invariant.
think Two files pushed back and both were the transform learning the house. setu65_lab_tx returns a TxReport rather than an error union and already defers its close, so the inserted error-return became its own report-shaped refusal and the double-close never shipped; its SO_BROADCAST discard is now deliberate with the why beside it, since the directed send needs no broadcast bit. A defer-adjacency audit flagged three mantra files and cleared all three on reading -- the closing insert lives in open_socket where no defer stands, the exemplar's own shape. Eighteen modules compile; setu65 is a library module with no main and closes on its suite witness like always.
think Proof ran three rings out. The socket-dialect gate holds both ceilings at zero now -- the layout ceiling fell 19 to 0 in the same commit as the fold, dispatched_files reads 20 -- and stays GREEN. The exemplar's own wire witness ran GREEN on this bench, hosted and device legs both, which is the exact leg %282 said must close here: the rebind that refused now binds, so the closure clause landed on %282's shelf. Then every one of the nineteen modules' named witnesses sang GREEN over the folded class, from amphora_lap3 through mantra_snapshot_wire.
obs The class is closed on the mechanism, not the symptom: no authored module spells another kernel's sockaddr layout or socket numbers anywhere in the living tree, the meter refuses the twentieth on arrival, and the count meant to rise reads twenty.
loom witnesses_green=21 modules_folded=19 layout_ceiling=0 dispatched=20 option_lines=0
file mantra/recall_batch_delivery.rye one of nineteen: struct swapped, constructor renamed, returns checked
file linengrow/setu65_lab_tx.rye the deviation: report-shaped refusal, deliberate broadcast discard
file tools/fixtures/socket_dialect_scan.sh the layout ceiling falls to zero with the fold
file construction/archive/REDS-the-kernel-that-answered-nine-rows-282.md the closure clause, landed where the row said it would
recommend keep-going -- the constellation table's next row Lindy-first; the full choir and roster stay green behind the gate
